      "type": "reassess",
      "args": {},
      "justification": "Inhalation injury significantly increases mortality and fluid requirements in burn patients. Early identification of signs (singed nasal hairs, carbonaceous sputum, hoarseness, facial burns) is critical to guide further management including possible bronchoscopy."
